[
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we have a convention for spacing around <code>¬</code>?<br>\n(I don't think we necessarily need one but if one exists I want to follow it)</p>",
        "id": 627470377,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1790608462
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think mathlib has a uniform convention. I personally like \"no space in front of simple expressions (like a literal <code>¬p</code>), but space in front of more complicated ones\". I look even more forward to an auto-formatter handling this for me. I'm optimistic that we'll have a version available for trial in mathlib by the end of the year (but this might be an optimistic estimate).</p>",
        "id": 627471578,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1790608678
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah I want a tool to make these sort of formatting decisions for me. Personally I've been always spacing, but I don't actually care.</p>",
        "id": 627471851,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1790608722
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FWIW 60% of Mathlib usage is spaceless, so the trend is no space<br>\n(but I haven't partitioned by simple/complex expressions)</p>",
        "id": 627472447,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1790608830
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What's the sample size?</p>",
        "id": 627472556,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1790608851
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here is an estimate of the current count:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">cghenson</span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">cghenson</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">~/</span><span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">mathlib4</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">ho</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'¬</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">/.*/</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&amp;\"</span><span class=\"bp\">/'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uniq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">nr</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"mi\">3409</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"¬\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"mi\">2166</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"¬ \"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"¬   \"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 627472580,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1790608857
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p><code>      2 \"¬   \"</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>!!</p>",
        "id": 627472712,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1790608877
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That is in <code>MathlibTest/PPRoundtrip.lean</code>, so probably intentional</p>",
        "id": 627473049,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1790608940
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The pretty printing is also spaceless, so maybe the upcoming autoformatter will do the same? (Not sure if that's actually how it works)</p>",
        "id": 627474268,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1790609166
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"687698\">Chris Henson</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/.60.C2.AC.60.20spacing/near/627472580\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Here is an estimate of the current count:</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This will be heavily biased by what mathport decided to convert the lean3 code to.</p>",
        "id": 627475192,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1790609354
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"687698\">Chris Henson</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/.60.C2.AC.60.20spacing/near/627473049\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That is in <code>MathlibTest/PPRoundtrip.lean</code>, so probably intentional</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Looking at this linter, I see it does something similar to what I was speculating about with pretty printing (so complains about the space). It's off by default presumably because there are many places this isn't followed and/or performance.</p>",
        "id": 627477992,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1790609963
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The new autoformatter adds a space if the operand is not atomic or self-delimited, so e.g. applications get a space but constants don't and parentheses don't either:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">opaque</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">¬</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 627514703,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790618616
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/mhuisi/lean4/blob/33c055b97339886987a08b48c2aa8e4d55c122a2/src/Lean/Fmt/FmtM/Layouts.lean#L308\">for reference</a></p>",
        "id": 627515853,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1790618867
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43777\">#43777</a> (linter for redundant <code>&lt;|</code> syntax ) I implemented a check that seems similar to this check of being atomic or self delimited. Maybe I this should reuse the code from the formatter once we get it.</p>",
        "id": 627517064,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1790619157
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"¬   \"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Burn the heretic</p>",
        "id": 627541816,
        "sender_full_name": "aerh",
        "timestamp": 1790625434
    }
]